stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Selecting: run
  Selecting --> Refused: refusal, timeout or signal
  Selecting --> Committed: handoff attempt recorded
  Committed --> NotExecuted: signal at the linearization point
  Committed --> LaunchFailed: harness cannot be started
  Committed --> Running: harness spawned as a job
  Running --> Reaped: harness exits on its own
  Running --> Grace: exit channel appears
  Grace --> Reaped: harness exits within 2 s
  Grace --> Terminating: SIGTERM to group H
  Terminating --> Reaped: harness exits
  Terminating --> Killed: SIGKILL after 5 s
  Killed --> Reaped
  Running --> Cancelling: INT, TERM or HUP to dispatch
  Grace --> Cancelling: INT, TERM or HUP to dispatch
  Terminating --> Cancelling: INT, TERM or HUP to dispatch
  Cancelling --> Reaped: same signal, then KILL after 5 s (confined, KILL at once)
  Reaped --> Recorded: restore terminal, append end observation, write ending file
  Recorded --> [*]: exit per the ending
  Refused --> [*]: no run, no ending
  NotExecuted --> [*]: attempt marked not executed, no ending
  LaunchFailed --> [*]: launch failure recorded, no ending
  note right of Reaped
    Ending: cancelled if dispatch was signalled,
    else exit_signal if the channel exists,
    else harness_exit
  end note
